    'svc.audit-log.overview':                        'Every module records its activity here instead of scattering audit rows through its own database. Events are append-only, and each one’s SHA-256 hash covers both its own content and the previous event’s hash, so the log is a chain: rewriting, removing or reordering any past event breaks every hash after it. The chain head is recorded with each append, which also catches events deleted from the end — the edit a hash chain alone cannot see. GET /api/verify recomputes the whole chain and reports how it broke. Retention pruning re-anchors the chain rather than severing it.',
